.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH dx 1  "dx 0.0.0" 
.SH NAME
dx \- Run Bazel workflows
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdx\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
dx <command> [flags] [scope ...] [\-\- bazel\-options ...]
.PP
Scopes: labels, patterns, files, or dirs. No scope means //... for most commands.
.PP
Exit codes: 0 success, 2 usage error, 1 failed check.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
dx\-security(1)
run security audit over resolved scopes (non\-mutating; live Gitleaks plus advisory/vuln backends)
.TP
dx\-license(1)
run license audit over resolved scopes (non\-mutating; live license\-policy plus SPDX backend)
.TP
dx\-lint(1)
run lint analysis over resolved scopes (check by default; \-\-apply writes fixes)
.TP
dx\-typecheck(1)
run typecheck analysis over resolved scopes (check by default; \-\-apply writes fixes)
.TP
dx\-format(1)
check or rewrite formatting over resolved scopes (check by default; \-\-apply writes fixes)
.TP
dx\-generate(1)
emit/sync BUILD files (Gazelle pipeline; check by default; \-\-apply writes generated sources)
.TP
dx\-build(1)
run Bazel build over resolved targets
.TP
dx\-test(1)
run Bazel test over resolved targets
.TP
dx\-coverage(1)
collect LCOV coverage with optional threshold
.TP
dx\-run(1)
build and run runnable targets sequentially (explicit labels/patterns; file/dir scopes need exactly one runnable)
.TP
dx\-deploy(1)
build and run a single deployable target
.TP
dx\-check(1)
run format+lint+typecheck+generate checks in order (non\-mutating)
.TP
dx\-fix(1)
apply format+lint+typecheck+generate fixes in order (check by default; \-\-apply writes fixes, then verifies with a read\-only check)
.TP
dx\-clean(1)
prune unselected managed state, never Bazel outputs unless \-\-bazel (check by default; \-\-apply prunes; no scopes)
.TP
dx\-update(1)
update dependencies per set through qualified resolvers (mutating without confirmation; \-\-check validates selected sets without writing)
.TP
dx\-bump(1)
widen one declared requirement to a new version (explicit; mutating without confirmation)
.TP
dx\-migrate(1)
rewrite breaking changes across releases (upgrade\-only; mutating by default; \-\-dry\-run plans without writes)
.TP
dx\-codegen(1)
collect codegen outputs with atomic commit (check by default; \-\-apply writes managed state)
.TP
dx\-env(1)
collect the managed development environment (check by default; \-\-apply writes managed state)
.TP
dx\-setup(1)
collect setup outputs with atomic commit (check by default; \-\-apply writes managed state)
.TP
dx\-init(1)
scaffold dx into a foreign tree (absent\-only; mutating by default)
.TP
dx\-new(1)
scaffold a minimal qualified project for one language (absent\-only; mutating by default)
.TP
dx\-upgrade(1)
one\-shot pin+migrate+setup composition with recovery pointer (mutating by default; \-\-dry\-run plans without writes)
.TP
dx\-hooks(1)
manage Git hooks via hermetic Git (mutating by default)
.TP
dx\-status(1)
report workspace and target status
.TP
dx\-version(1)
report version and pin drift
.TP
dx\-watch(1)
watch for changes and rebuild (local only)
.TP
dx\-owners(1)
query owners of files via Bazel query
.TP
dx\-deps(1)
query dependencies of targets
.TP
dx\-why(1)
explain why a target depends on another
.TP
dx\-completion(1)
emit shell completions from the CLI grammar (bash|zsh|fish|powershell; \-\-check verifies without writing)
.TP
dx\-docs(1)
build, check, and serve the mdBook documentation site (non\-mutating; \-\-check validates without rendering)
.TP
dx\-bazel(1)
forward raw arguments to the Bazel launcher
.SH VERSION
v0.0.0
